    20	// Named component rather than an inline `render: () => { useState(...) }`. A lowercase `render`
    21	// is not a component as far as eslint-plugin-react-hooks is concerned, so calling a hook inside
    22	// it trips react-hooks/rules-of-hooks. Behaviour is identical — this story ignores `args`, and
    23	// controls derive from `meta.component`, not from `render`.
